  "provenance": {
    "spawn": "func_080E8E74 follows each gUnk_09EF8388 world list until the first entry with unk_00 equal41. The array includes that consumed sentinel. Entries are native eight-byte chance records, not graphics assets.",
    "events": "func_080E9078 follows each gUnk_09EF83C0 world list until the first four-byte entry whose unk_00[0] is4. Each definition includes the consumed sentinel and stops before the next independently indexed list.",
    "native_catalog": "The thirteen sentinel-terminated chance lists and thirteen sentinel-terminated event lists bracket a256-byte typed data run. Existing code independently indexes40 card-prize records, including explicit reads of records38 and39, and19 stock-prize records whose IDs140..158 terminate at an independently addressed ten-halfword random-weight table. The world event lists reach stock index18. The random reader loops exactly10times and its original weights sum10000. These three bounded definitions complete the existing map-spawn catalog, whose ordinary initialized-data order reproduces all1948original bytes in every region. The weights use mutable definition storage to match the existing surrounding typed catalog arrays; this is a source reconstruction inference, not evidence of runtime writes or proof of original qualification. The reader retains its const pointer view. The former record14 address alias becomes a direct expression within the actual card array, and the stock-array reference replaces arithmetic across the card-array boundary. No element values, layouts, sentinels, extents of existing objects, data assets, or unknown field names change. All types remain in map.h; shared declarations belong to map_spawn_data.h. Five unrelated tile-loading expressions formerly escaped far beyond the ten weights; these now reference three actual bounded tile objects in the unchanged following asset stream. Their sizes1536/6144/2432 follow the complete tile spans selected by the existing2/15/8 Sprite tables. Each begins immediately after its last complete AnimHeader and ends at the next independently referenced Sprite, retaining the final two alignment bytes outside the third object. Existing binary-asset materialization emits real sized OBJECT labels with direct C relocations; no payload or source section placement is added."
  },
